"Create ONE self-contained SVG illustration of a small mind-map subtree about \"Coffee\". Reply with ONLY the SVG markup (no code fence, no commentary).\n\nCONTRACT (hard requirements):\n- Root element: <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 800 600\"> (no width/height needed).\n- Exactly one <g> per node, with id=\"node-<id>\" and attributes data-anchor-in=\"x,y\" and data-anchor-out=\"x,y\" (absolute viewBox coordinates; the point where a connector enters / leaves the node artwork). All artwork for a node must be drawn inside its own group and stay inside that node's target box.\n- Nodes (id, title, target box x,y,w,h):\n  n1 \"Coffee\"   box 300,240,200,120  (root, centre)\n  n2 \"Origins\"  box 40,40,220,140    (top-left)\n  n3 \"Brewing\"  box 540,40,220,140   (top-right)\n  n4 \"Beans\"    box 40,420,220,140   (bottom-left)\n  n5 \"Roasting\" box 540,420,220,140  (bottom-right)\n  The artwork of each node should depict what its title means (e.g. a cup for Coffee, a globe/mountain for Origins, a dripper/kettle for Brewing, beans for Beans, a flame/drum for Roasting).\n- Connectors from n1 to n2..n5 may be drawn in an extra <g id=\"connectors\"> outside the node groups.\n- Forbidden: <script>, <text>, <image>, <foreignObject>, external references (href/xlink:href to anything other than \"#id\"), url() other than local gradients, CSS @import. No <text> at all: the app draws labels.\n- At most 60 <path> elements in total. Other primitives (rect, circle, ellipse, polygon, line) allowed.\n- Use only this 5-colour palette (hex): #3B2417, #8B5A2B, #D9A066, #F2E3C6, #E4572E. No other colours.\n"